<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<sdf version="1.9">
  <!--
    testworld_simple: a Nav2 world sized against THIS robot, created 2026-08-21.

    testworld_v1 is not passable for it. Circumscribed radius is 0.378 m, so the
    machine needs 0.756 m of clear width, and nav2.yaml inflates every obstacle
    by inflation_radius 0.50 m. Measured against that, testworld_v1 contains:
      corridor_barrel at (0, -3.4)   0.62 m either side  -> BLOCKS the corridor
      chicane at y 2.9..3.8          0.80 m              -> 44 mm total clearance
      pillar_sw_corridor             0.97 m              -> fully inflated
      room-to-room doors             1.20 m              -> under 2x inflation_radius
    The corridor is therefore closed to this robot south of y = -3.4, which is
    the half the (0, -5) spawn sits in.

    Design rule here: EVERY passage is at least 2.0 m wide — 0.5 m of inflation
    per side plus a 1.0 m corridor of low cost down the middle, so the planner
    has a genuinely free lane rather than a least-bad one.

    Layout (top view, x east, y north, origin at world centre):
      12x12 m arena, closed outer walls, identical to testworld_v1 so the
      (0, -5) spawn and spawn_yaw 1.5708 carry over unchanged.
      One divider across y = 0 with a single 2.0 m gate at x in [-1.0, +1.0],
      straight ahead of the spawn.
      Two pillars (r 0.25) and two crates, each well clear of walls and gate.

    No saved map exists for this world: use localization:=slam (the default).
    localization:=amcl loads testworld_v1's map and will not match.
  -->
  <world name="testworld_simple">
    <gravity>0 0 -9.81</gravity>
    <physics name="1ms" type="ignored">
      <!-- 0.001 -> 0.010 on 2026-08-24 (user decision), i.e. 100 Hz physics.
           MEASURED headless with the real model in testworld_v1, startup cost
           subtracted, 2 runs each: the cost per step is flat at ~1.0 ms
           regardless of step size, so the load scales linearly with the step
           COUNT. Max achievable real-time factor:
               0.001 -> 0.98-1.03x     0.002 -> 2.07-2.21x
               0.004 -> 3.77-4.01x     0.010 -> 9.97-11.59x
           At 0.001 the physics had NO headroom at all -- 1.0x headless, with no
           rendering, no gz_ros2_control, no bridge, no Nav2, no RViz. That is
           why the sim felt slow: real_time_factor 1.0 throttles the server to
           real time, and it was sitting exactly on that limit.

           WHY THIS IS AFFORDABLE HERE, and it is a statement about THIS model:
           a fine step buys fidelity only where there is stiff, tuned contact
           dynamics to resolve. There is none. Total simulated mass is 3.72 kg
           (arm_stowed_link weighs 1 GRAM, imu_link likewise, and chassis_link's
           2.27 kg is bare CAD shell -- no battery, Pi, motors or electronics);
           the real mass is not documented anywhere (internal REQUIREMENTS S25/HWR-32,
           "No CG/weight budget"). There is not one friction or contact
           parameter in the whole workspace -- no mu, mu2, slip, kp/kd, no
           <surface> -- so every tyre is Gazebo default on a smooth cylinder.
           Integrating placeholder numbers ten times more finely buys nothing.

           STABILITY, measured: dropped from 0.20 m onto the ground plane, the
           model settles 0.074 mm lower than at 0.001, with 0.33 mm of residual
           jitter and no tilt. Sub-millimetre against a 70 mm wheel radius.

           WHAT THIS DOES COST -- control-period jitter, see the note in
           gripperx_control/config/ros2_controllers.yaml (update_rate: 30).
           100 Hz does not divide by 30. ros2_control can only fire on a physics
           tick, so the 33.3 ms period becomes an alternating 30/40 ms one
           (-10 %/+20 %); at 0.001 the same quantisation was +-1.5 %. The period
           handed to the controllers is the true elapsed one, so odometry
           integration stays correct -- but any fixed-gain filter or rate limiter
           tuned at a steady 30 Hz now sees a varying period.
           1/120 s (0.008333) would divide 30 Hz exactly, giving ~8.3x instead
           of ~10x for zero jitter, if that trade is ever worth making. -->
      <max_step_size>0.010</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1.0</real_time_factor>
    </physics>

    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-physics-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::Physics" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-user-commands-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::UserCommands" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-scene-broadcaster-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-contact-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::Contact" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-imu-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::Imu" />
    <plugin
      filename="gz-sim-sensors-system"
      name="gz::sim::systems::Sensors">
      <render_engine>ogre2</render_engine>
    </plugin>

    <light name="sun" type="directional">
      <!-- Shadows off 2026-08-24. A shadow map is a second full render pass over
           the scene per light, and on the development laptop's Intel UHD 620 that
           is paid for every GUI frame and every sensor frame. Nothing in this
           project reads shadows: the LiDAR is a gpu_lidar (range only, unlit) and
           no node subscribes to the camera. Purely cosmetic cost, so it is off by
           default. Set back to true if a scenario ever needs a lit image. -->
      <cast_shadows>false</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 12 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular>
      <attenuation>
        <range>1000</range>
        <constant>0.9</constant>
        <linear>0.01</linear>
        <quadratic>0.001</quadratic>
      </attenuation>
      <direction>-0.5 0.1 -0.9</direction>
    </light>

    <model name="ground_plane">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>60 60</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>60 60</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.78 0.78 0.78 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.78 0.78 0.78 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="outer_wall_north">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 6 1.0 0 0 0.0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>12.2 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>12.2 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.55 0.55 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.65 0.65 0.7 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="outer_wall_south">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>0 -6 1.0 0 0 0.0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>12.2 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>12.2 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.55 0.55 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.65 0.65 0.7 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="outer_wall_east">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>6 0 1.0 0 0 0.0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>0.2 12.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>0.2 12.2 2.0</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.55 0.55 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.65 0.65 0.7 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="outer_wall_west">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>-6 0 1.0 0 0 0.0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>0.2 12.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>0.2 12.2 2.0</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.55 0.55 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.65 0.65 0.7 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="divider_west">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>-3.55 0 1.0 0 0 0.0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>5.1 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>5.1 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.55 0.55 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.65 0.65 0.7 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="divider_east">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>3.55 0 1.0 0 0 0.0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>5.1 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>5.1 0.2 2.0</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.55 0.55 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.65 0.65 0.7 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="pillar_north">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>-2.6 3.0 0.6 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><cylinder><radius>0.25</radius><length>1.2</length></cylinder></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.25</radius><length>1.2</length></cylinder></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.6 0.4 0.25 1</ambient><diffuse>0.7 0.5 0.3 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="pillar_south">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>2.6 -3.0 0.6 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><cylinder><radius>0.25</radius><length>1.2</length></cylinder></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><cylinder><radius>0.25</radius><length>1.2</length></cylinder></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.6 0.4 0.25 1</ambient><diffuse>0.7 0.5 0.3 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="crate_nw">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>-5.5 5.5 0.3 0 0 0.0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>0.8 0.8 0.6</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>0.8 0.8 0.6</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.55 0.55 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.65 0.65 0.7 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="crate_se">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>5.5 -5.5 0.3 0 0 0.0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision"><geometry><box><size>0.8 0.8 0.6</size></box></geometry></collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry><box><size>0.8 0.8 0.6</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.55 0.55 0.6 1</ambient><diffuse>0.65 0.65 0.7 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

  </world>
</sdf>
